      },
      {
        "index": 5,
        "blockIndex": 1,
        "paragraphInBlock": 0,
        "text": "Because of inertia, the object's tendency to keep its motion, a force can increase the oscillator's speed only gradually;\nwhen the force stops acting, the velocity does not immediately become zero."
